  "validate": "H59",
  "narrative": "This wave largely establishes robustness of the main accepted dataset associations across several biologically relevant contexts. H52-H54 restrict SMARCA4-loss versus non-loss for SMARCA2 dependency to adenocarcinoma, ARID1A-wild-type cells, and low-mutation-burden cells. In all three restrictions, the signed effect remains about +0.77 to +0.78 with narrow intervals far from zero. This argues against the simple explanations that the SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 association is driven only by lineage, ARID1A co-loss, or low mutation burden. I therefore accept H52-H54 as dataset-level robustness confirmations and close those investigations.\n\nH55-H56 restrict KEAP1-loss versus non-loss for NFE2L2 dependency to adherent culture and TP53-wild-type cells. The signed effects remain about +0.79 with tight intervals, showing that the large KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 association persists after these potential context or co-alteration restrictions. These are accepted and closed. H57-H58 restrict MSI-high versus non-MSI-high for WRN dependency to adherent culture and TP53-wild-type cells; the signed effects remain about +0.78 to +0.81 and precise. H34 additionally shows the MSI/WRN effect remains essentially unchanged within the dominant Avana screen library. Thus the MSI/WRN association is not merely a culture artifact, TP53-loss artifact, or Avana-library-specific screening artifact. These are accepted and closed.\n\nFor USP7, H44 shows the validated TP53-wild-type/TP53-loss association remains robust within the Avana library, with a signed effect about +0.40. This supports H44 and closes it. H59 restricts the TP53-wild-type/USP7 contrast to high mutation burden and yields a larger signed effect, about +0.48, with a precise interval well above clinical relevance. H60 restricts the contrast to KEAP1-wild-type cells and yields a signed effect about +0.37, also well above clinical relevance. These results suggest that the TP53-wild-type/USP7 association is robust to screening library and KEAP1 state and may be even stronger in higher mutation-burden contexts. I accept H60 and close it. I accept H59 but keep it active and request independent validation because it is a context-specific refinement with a large new point estimate; independent confirmation would be useful before closing it as a separate context association. This is not a causal claim: high mutation burden may correlate with MSI, DNA-repair defects, p53 pathway state, aneuploidy, or screening/context factors, and the observed modification could be confounded or biologically context dependent.\n\nH47 tests whether the borderline MSI-high/USP7 signal survives within TP53-wild-type cells. The signed estimate is only +0.032 and the interval crosses zero, [-0.003, +0.068]. The point estimate is much smaller than the main accepted associations, and the uncertainty is insufficient to support a clinically meaningful MSI-high/USP7 association. Combined with the earlier borderline H39 result, I leave H47 unresolved but close it, and I close H39 as well to reduce low-priority follow-up. The evidence does not support accepting MSI-high as a robust predictor of USP7 dependency in this dataset.\n\nOverall, the strongest conclusions remain dataset-level associations: SMARCA4 loss associates with stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1 loss associates with weaker/higher NFE2L2 dependency; MSI-high associates with stronger WRN dependency; and TP53-wild-type status associates with stronger USP7 dependency. The new results make these effects much less attributable to lineage subtype, ARID1A co-loss, low mutation burden, culture type, TP53-loss co-state, Avana library, or KEAP1 co-state. Residual confounding remains possible due to unmeasured pathway interactions, batch, screen quality, growth rate, media, ploidy, or co-alteration structure, and no result should be interpreted as causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted main dataset associations: H9 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H13 KEAP1 loss -> weaker/higher NFE2L2 dependency; H10 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H15 TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency with independent validation. New robustness acceptances: SMARCA4/SMARCA2 persists in adenocarcinoma (H52), ARID1A wild-type (H53), and low mutation burden (H54). KEAP1/NFE2L2 persists in adherent culture (H55) and TP53 wild-type (H56). MSI/WRN persists in adherent culture (H57), TP53 wild-type (H58), and Avana library (H34). TP53 wild-type/USP7 persists in Avana (H44) and KEAP1 wild-type (H60). H59 shows a large TP53 wild-type/USP7 effect in high mutation burden and has been accepted provisionally but kept active pending independent validation. H47 and H39 are borderline/negative for MSI-high/USP7: effects are small and intervals cross zero; both closed unresolved. Do not interpret these as causal or generalizable; context restrictions reduce some confounding candidates but cannot rule out unmeasured biology or screen artifacts. Next priority: assess validation for H59 in synthesis, then continue broad exploration using untested pending claims and interactions rather than low-priority USP7-MSI follow-up."
}

{
  "validate": "H9",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted main dataset associations: H9 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H13 KEAP1 loss -> weaker/higher NFE2L2 dependency; H10 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; H15 TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency with independent validation. H36 and H59 provide validated/robust context confirmations for KEAP1/NFE2L2 in Avana and TP53 wild-type/USP7 in higher mutation burden, respectively. H4 EGFR amplification/EGFR dependency is rejected after near-null validation. The main remaining validation gaps are H9 SMARCA4/SMARCA2 and H10 MSI/WRN. This appraise requests independent validation of H9 first because it is a strong, broadly accepted main effect with adequate cell sizes and has not yet received independent validation. If H9 validates, H10 should be considered next. Interpret all findings as dataset associations only, not causal or externally generalizable.",
  "narrative": "No newly listed discovery evidence currently requires changing an accepted or active claim status. The most scientifically valuable action in this appraise slot is to request independent validation of H9, the SMARCA4-loss versus non-loss contrast for SMARCA2 dependency. H9 is a central accepted dataset association with a large signed effect and it has already survived several contextual robustness checks, but it remains without independent validation. Replicating H9 on an independent validation split would help distinguish a reproducible dataset-level association from discovery-sample noise, especially before treating this claim as one of the strongest synthetic-lethality-like associations in this screen. I defer validation of H10 MSI-high/WRN for a subsequent request because only one voluntary validation is allowed here and H9 has larger exposure/comparator cell sizes, making its validation more likely to be informative if successful. This validation request does not imply causality or external generalizability; it tests reproducibility within the supplied evidence framework."
}

