  "narrative": "The newly delivered validation substantially strengthens the central evidence set. H10 (MSI-high versus MSI-stable for dependency_WRN) now has independent validation: discovery R10 was a signed +0.790 (95% CI +0.760 to +0.819), and validation R66 is +0.812 with an independent interval +0.765 to +0.858. Because the claim direction is -1, these signed positive values mean MSI-high cells have more negative WRN scores, i.e., stronger WRN dependency. The validation interval excludes zero and the effect is far larger than the small effects seen in rejected null claims, so I accept H10 and close it as a robust within-dataset association. H36 (KEAP1 loss versus KEAP1 wild-type for dependency_NFE2L2 within Avana-library screens) is also independently validated: discovery R21 +0.796 (CI +0.774 to +0.818) and validation R40 +0.795 (independent CI +0.764 to +0.826). With direction +1, positive values indicate KEAP1-loss cells have higher NFE2L2 dependency scores, i.e., weaker NFE2L2 dependency. I accept and close H36 as a well-supported Avana-subset association. H59 (TP53 wild-type versus TP53-loss for dependency_USP7 among high mutation-burden cells) is independently validated as well: discovery R34 +0.477 (CI +0.379 to +0.576) and validation R39 +0.392 (independent CI +0.239 to +0.545). The validation estimate is somewhat smaller than discovery but still large, positive, and far above zero. I accept and close H59. These results, together with the already validated H9 (SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency) and H15 (TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency), give four internally reproducible dataset-level associations: SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency; KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency; and TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency. For H13, the unrestricted KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 association remains accepted and active because the exact unrestricted claim has not yet received direct independent validation, although it is strongly supported by R8 discovery and by H36's independent Avana-subset validation. The most informative next step is therefore to obtain direct independent validation for H13 if eligible, while analyzing the already registered non-Avana robustness claims and mutation-burden interactions. Negative or unsupported findings include the expected KEAP1-loss stronger-NFE2L2 hypothesis in H8, EGFR amplification/EGFR dependency in H4, BRAF V600E/BRAF dependency in H3, ARID1A loss/SMARCA2 dependency in H14, TP53 status/RPL11 dependency in H16, research-marker associations in H42 and H43, and the rejected interaction claims H112-H114 showing little modification of the main SMARCA2, NFE2L2, and WRN effects by MSI-high or SMARCA4 loss. Unresolved uncertainty remains for non-Avana library replication, mutation-burden interactions, USP7 modified by MYC amplification (H115, positive but wide interval), and external generalizability or causal mechanism. I registered new co-alteration-exclusion refinements to ask whether the main associations persist when the other major accepted predictor state is excluded (KEAP1 wild-type for SMARCA2 and WRN; MSI wild-type for USP7 and NFE2L2), while keeping all claims as dataset-level associations rather than causal claims.",
