  "narrative": "The delivered validations substantially strengthen the central evidence set and allow several key conclusions to be closed as dataset-level associations. H9 receives its direct independent validation response: discovery R9 and validation R53 are both large positive signed estimates under the negative direction, with validation R53 +0.804 and an independent interval +0.775 to +0.833. Because a signed positive value here corresponds to a more negative SMARCA2 dependency score in SMARCA4-loss cells, I accept H9 and close it: SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency in this dataset. The effect is far larger than the practical threshold used for these comparisons and is much larger than the null-like estimates seen in rejected comparisons. H13 now has direct independent validation of the unrestricted KEAP1-loss association: discovery R8 +0.796 and validation R79 +0.791, with the independent interval +0.763 to +0.820 excluding zero. Under direction +1, a positive signed estimate means KEAP1-loss cells have higher, less negative NFE2L2 dependency scores. I therefore accept and close H13 as evidence that KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency. The same validation also reinforces rejection of H8, the earlier stronger-dependency hypothesis, so the supported association is in the opposite direction of H8. H14, ARID1A loss versus SMARCA2 dependency, now has direct validation that is essentially null: R80 is -0.002 with interval -0.062 to +0.058. This is small relative to the supported central effects and not clinically meaningful, so I reject and close H14. Together, the direct validations support a core reproducible pattern in this dataset: SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, and TP53 wild-type status is associated with stronger USP7 dependency. These are associations measured across many subset, library, screen-quality, and co-alteration restrictions, but they are not claims about causality or external generalizability. Negative or unsupported findings remain important: BRAF V600E does not support a BRAF-dependency association, EGFR amplification does not support a meaningful EGFR-dependency association, ARID1A loss does not support an SMARCA2-dependency association, and the tested research-marker comparisons are null or nonmeaningful. Interaction tests for major effect modification by MSI-high, SMARCA4 loss, or ARID1A status are also unsupported for the central SMARCA2, NFE2L2, and WRN associations. The main unresolved uncertainty is not whether the central associations exist in this dataset, but whether their magnitude is constant across genomic and screen context. The TP53/USP7 effect is robust in Avana, high mutation burden, and several co-alteration exclusions, but appears smaller in some Ky-library analyses, leaving H123 unresolved and H75 accepted with magnitude caution. The new proposal asks whether the TP53 wild-type USP7 effect is specifically attenuated in the Ky library relative to the complement, which is the most direct follow-up to that caveat. The next most informative analyses are therefore the registered mutation-burden interactions and remaining library or co-alteration subsets for the four central associations, not additional weak marker screening.",
  "research_notes": "Updated evidence state after validation: H9 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency accepted and closed with direct validation R53. H10 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency remains accepted/closed with validation R66. H15 TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency remains accepted/closed with validation R26. H13 unrestricted KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency now accepted and closed with direct validation R79; H36 Avana subset also validated. H8 opposite KEAP1-loss stronger NFE2L2 hypothesis rejected and closed, with validation R79 confirming opposite direction. H14 ARID1A loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency rejected and closed with validation R80 near null. Central accepted dataset-level associations: SMARCA4 loss/stronger SMARCA2, MSI-high/stronger WRN, KEAP1 loss/weaker NFE2L2, TP53 wild-type/stronger USP7. Robustness subsets accepted/closed for these associations include Avana, non-Avana for SMARCA2/NFE2L2, Ky for SMARCA2/NFE2L2, adenocarcinoma, TP53 wild-type, KEAP1 wild-type, MSI stable, screen quality halves, media high, batch_a, high mutation burden for USP7, and several co-alteration exclusions. Negative/closed: H3 BRAF V600E/BRAF, H4 validated EGFR ampl/EGFR, H8 validated opposite NFE2L2 direction, H14 validated ARID1A/SMARCA2 null, H16 RPL11 null, H42/H43 research markers, H112-H114 interactions. Open caveats: USP7 effect size in Ky (H123 unresolved) and non-Avana small cell H75; mutation-burden interactions H80-H83 and direct high/low MB subsets; Humagne library subsets H124/H125; ARID1A WT exclusions H127/H129; WRN MSI outside Avana/Ky likely cell-size limited. New proposal registered: TP53 wild-type USP7 effect interaction by Ky library versus complement to test attenuation suggested by R69/R72. All conclusions remain within-dataset associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
}

